| `tests/integration/test_assertion_quality_gate.py` | Fails, at its file, line and function, a test function with no assertion in its body or in a helper it calls, with only truthy-constant assertions, with a tautology (a statically true expression or structurally identical adjacent comparison operands), or with a handler in its body that only passes or continues, so a test that cannot fail never reads as evidence. An assertion is an `assert`, a `pytest.raises` or `pytest.warns` block or call, a `pytest.fail` call, a mock's `assert_*` call, or `assert<Upper...>` / `fail` on a bound `unittest.TestCase` receiver (including aliases and local inheritance, calls and expectation blocks). The receiver is the first positional parameter, whatever its name, of a function defined directly in the class body, without a default or a `staticmethod` or `classmethod` decorator and with no other binding of that name. A name bound exactly once by `=` or `:=` to a receiver, or by a `for` or comprehension over a tuple or list display containing only receivers, counts too; any other binding or more than one rejects it. A generator's first iterable counts when constructed; its deferred calls count only when consumed by a running `for`, list, set or dict comprehension, `*`, `yield from`, a consumed outer generator, or an unrebound bare callee in `test_quality.assertions.consumers` in the configured `only` or `first` position. A singly bound generator name counts the same. Calls with keywords or argument unpacking never qualify. Positional `assertTrue`, `assertFalse` and `assertEqual` arguments use the expression judge; other TestCase assertions count without expression analysis; a comparison of two calls is a determinism check, never a tautology. Each configured root must exist and yield a test file. A run over zero test functions and a stale excuse fail too. Invalid policy values raise `SourceTreeError` with the loader's diagnostic lines and key names. | `make test` | [`test_quality.assertions.roots`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`test_quality.assertions.helper_depth`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`test_quality.assertions.consumers`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`test_quality.assertions.exempt.<test>`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | It reads the syntax tree and never runs a test: control flow can prevent a credited assertion from executing, and a handler that swallows inside a helper can pass. Not for a test or helper that is itself a generator function (queued). Generator arguments of attribute calls, unlisted callees or other call shapes receive no credit; argument values and control flow between bindings are not judged. Helpers reached through fixtures or variables, or in modules outside the roots, are not followed; a test whose only assertion is there fails as having no assertion. Not proof that an assertion is strong: a bare `isinstance` counts. Not mutation testing. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
